00:05:58.357 --> 00:05:59.559
and not what happens
to the targets.

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:01.059
Josh, you're up first.
Are you ready?

00:06:01.126 --> 00:06:01.861
 Nope.

00:06:01.928 --> 00:06:03.195
No.

00:06:03.262 --> 00:06:03.963
[bleep]

00:06:11.237 --> 00:06:12.638
Well, here's my finish.

00:06:20.246 --> 00:06:21.981
[bleep]

00:06:22.047 --> 00:06:22.949
 All right, Josh.

00:06:23.015 --> 00:06:24.283
Well, it survived really well.

00:06:24.350 --> 00:06:26.719
There is sections
on here that are

00:06:26.785 --> 00:06:28.221
now not as sharp as they were.

00:06:28.287 --> 00:06:30.723
But nothing rolled over,
nothing chipped out.

00:06:30.756 --> 00:06:32.658
Your point is still
nice and sharp.

00:06:32.725 --> 00:06:34.393
It performed really well
on the Strength Test.

00:06:34.459 --> 00:06:35.661
Nice job.
- Awesome.

00:06:35.695 --> 00:06:36.629
Thank you.

00:06:36.695 --> 00:06:37.930
 All right, Brad, are
you ready for this?

00:06:37.997 --> 00:06:39.799
 Well, my nan said don't
break it, but go for it.

00:06:54.914 --> 00:06:57.216
BEN ABBOTT: Well, Brad,
what you got here,

00:06:57.283 --> 00:06:59.585
your blade edge
took some damage.

00:06:59.652 --> 00:07:02.154
The blade has taken a bit
of a bend to one side here.

00:07:02.221 --> 00:07:03.289
It's cheating to the right.

00:07:03.355 --> 00:07:05.524
But your point didn't
take any damage.

00:07:05.591 --> 00:07:06.558
It's all in one piece.

00:07:06.625 --> 00:07:07.860
It's a nice sturdy blade.

00:07:07.927 --> 00:07:08.360
Nice job.

00:07:08.427 --> 00:07:09.429
 Thank you.

00:07:12.564 --> 00:07:14.633
 All right, bladesmiths,
this is the Sharpness

00:07:14.699 --> 00:07:16.835
Test, the Military Bag Slice.

00:07:16.902 --> 00:07:20.306
To find out how sharp your edges
and point of your bayonets are,

00:07:20.373 --> 00:07:22.842
I'm gonna take a stab
at these military bags.

00:07:22.909 --> 00:07:24.343
Josh, you're up first.
You ready?

00:07:24.409 --> 00:07:25.111
 Let's go for it.

00:07:39.592 --> 00:07:41.727
 All right, Josh,
your bayonet right

00:07:41.794 --> 00:07:44.463
here had no problems
puncturing the bag

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:46.765
and slicing it to pieces.

00:07:46.832 --> 00:07:47.733
It'll cut.

00:07:47.766 --> 00:07:48.300
 Sweet.

00:07:48.367 --> 00:07:49.502
Thanks.

00:07:49.569 --> 00:07:51.036
 All right, Brad,
your turn, sir.

00:07:51.103 --> 00:07:51.937
Shall we do it?

00:07:52.004 --> 00:07:52.538
 Of course.

00:07:52.571 --> 00:07:53.473
Have at you.

00:08:05.884 --> 00:08:07.119
 Pew, pew, pew.

00:08:07.186 --> 00:08:08.754
[laughter]

00:08:09.889 --> 00:08:12.792
All right, Brad, let's
talk about your blade here.

00:08:12.859 --> 00:08:13.792
Wicked sharp.

00:08:13.859 --> 00:08:15.828
It punctured easily
in the military bag.

00:08:15.861 --> 00:08:20.565
At the same time, the edges
cut like hot steel on butter.

00:08:20.632 --> 00:08:24.336
Overall, sir, for this
test, it will cut.

00:08:24.403 --> 00:08:26.838
 Thank you, sir.

00:08:26.905 --> 00:08:28.374
HOST: All right,
gentleman, while you

00:08:28.441 --> 00:08:30.843
both brought us amazing
work, only one of you

00:08:30.876 --> 00:08:32.711
